\id 3JN Transparent Bible (working title)
\h 3 John
\mt1 3 John
\c 1
\p
\v 1 The elder to the beloved Gaius, whom I love in truth.
\v 2 Beloved,\f + \fr 1:2 \ft Text: TR, Maj.: \fqa Beloved\ft . CT omits.\f* \wj I pray that all may go well with \+zpl you\+zpl*, \+add Gaius\+add*\wj*
\v 3 For I rejoiced greatly when brothers came and testified to your truth.
\v 4 I have no greater joy than to hear that my children are walking in the truth.
\v 5 Beloved, you are acting faithfully.
\v 6 They have testified to your love before the \nd LORD\nd*'s church.\f + \fr 1:6 \ft Heb.: \+nd LORD\+nd* is the divine name\f*
\v 7 For they have gone out for the sake of the Name.
\v 8 Therefore we ought to support such men.
\v 9 I wrote something to the church.
\v 10 Therefore, if I come, I will bring up what he is doing.
\v 11 Beloved, do not imitate evil.
\v 12 Demetrius has received a good testimony from everyone.
\v 13 I had much to write to you.
\v 14 I hope to see you soon.
